target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestCheckReadsOmittedBranchesFromGit'
expect: did not make main the default
why:    the default branch is the one the gate exists to protect, and an omitted -default-branch left it "" — a refusal for "branch unknown" on every branch, the default included, so the reason never named the real problem. Read from origin/HEAD, it refuses the default branch for the right reason and permits a feature branch.
--- old
	if defBranch == "" {
		defBranch = defaultBranch(p.Repo)
	}
--- new
